      "artist": "\"Generaldirektoratet for Postvaesenet\" of the Kingdom of Denmark",
      "description": "Stamp of the Kingdom of Denmark; 1907; definitive stamp of the issue \"King Frederick VIII of Denmark\", 1906 series, so-called \"Berlin Print\"; portrait of King Frederick VIII of Denmark with view to right; special characteristic of this issue (\"Berlin print\"): the background of the portrait-oval is striped by vertical and horizontal lines, whereas the 1904 issue (= type I) has only horizontal stripes; stamp postmarked in Skive, 1906\nStamp: Michel: No. 48II; Yvert et Tellier: No. 54; AFA: No. 53\nColor: red\nWatermark: Denmark No. 3 (Michel: 1Z) (new (oval) crown)\nNominal value: 10 Øre\n\nPostage validity: from March 1906 until 31 December 1926date QS:P,+1950-00-00T00:00:00Z/7,P580,+1906-03-00T00:00:00Z/10,P582,+1926-12-31T00:00:00Z/11\nStamp picture size (printed area): 17.0 x 20.0 mm (only at type II)\n\nPostmark: Skive (Region Midtjylland), 16 June 1906",
      "dateCreated": "1906-03",
